WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:03.270
Speaker 1: Okay, so let's start talking about reflogs.

00:03.270 --> 00:06.930
So the term reflogs is short for reference logs.

00:06.930 --> 00:09.690
And I recognize it doesn't sound

00:09.690 --> 00:12.840
very exciting at all or even that useful,

00:12.840 --> 00:15.840
but trust me, we will see how these come in handy.

00:15.840 --> 00:18.810
But they are just logs, they're just a transcript

00:18.810 --> 00:21.060
or a record that Git keeps for us

00:21.060 --> 00:23.550
of whenever references are updated.

00:23.550 --> 00:25.740
So references in Git,

00:25.740 --> 00:27.660
I've also used the term pointer,

00:27.660 --> 00:31.050
are things like this in my diagrams where I have an arrow.

00:31.050 --> 00:34.110
So a branch, every branch has a branch reference, right?

00:34.110 --> 00:36.450
That is what keeps the tip of the branch.

00:36.450 --> 00:39.210
So in my diagrams, it's been a name with an arrow

00:39.210 --> 00:40.620
pointing to a commit.

00:40.620 --> 00:43.710
Another reference we've seen would be HEAD.

00:43.710 --> 00:45.300
So HEAD can refer to a branch

00:45.300 --> 00:47.850
or it can point to a commit and detached HEAD.

00:47.850 --> 00:49.590
There are other references as well,

00:49.590 --> 00:51.840
things for remote branches.

00:51.840 --> 00:54.270
There's fetch HEAD, merge HEAD,

00:54.270 --> 00:56.400
there are different references in Git.

00:56.400 --> 01:00.240
So Git is going to keep a record of when they change

01:00.240 --> 01:02.280
and it actually stores them in a file.

01:02.280 --> 01:05.190
So in my diagrams here I'm kind of indicating the

01:05.190 --> 01:07.560
potential log for HEAD.

01:07.560 --> 01:11.430
So a reflog, a reference log for when HEAD changes.

01:11.430 --> 01:14.520
So here's HEAD in this hypothetical situation, it's pointing

01:14.520 --> 01:17.910
to Feature, which in turn is pointing to this commit.

01:17.910 --> 01:20.550
So then we make a new commit, commit H.

01:20.550 --> 01:22.560
I'm just using letters to make it simple.

01:22.560 --> 01:24.270
But then we switch branches.

01:24.270 --> 01:26.220
HEAD now points to Main.

01:26.220 --> 01:28.620
So Git actually takes note of that and it says,

01:28.620 --> 01:33.090
oh, you just switched HEAD, changed from Main to Feature,

01:33.090 --> 01:34.530
or other way around, I think.

01:34.530 --> 01:36.390
It changed to Main from Feature.

01:36.390 --> 01:39.540
And then if we switch back, Git takes note of that.

01:39.540 --> 01:42.690
You switched to the Feature branch from Main.

01:42.690 --> 01:44.760
So it has this running log.

01:44.760 --> 01:46.620
We haven't seen it yet, but there is a log,

01:46.620 --> 01:49.110
and there's actually a file that we can take a look at

01:49.110 --> 01:51.450
for HEAD if we want to see the reflog,

01:51.450 --> 01:54.360
the reference log in any repository.

01:54.360 --> 01:57.360
I'm using this react repository because it has

01:57.360 --> 01:58.800
a lot of history.

01:58.800 --> 02:00.720
If you wanna follow along, I would just work

02:00.720 --> 02:03.660
